  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\nNone of the ten multi-axis kinds takes a user start point or exit point. RotaryOffset and MultiAxisRough have `links` and refuse a pick (`sane.rs:71-87`). The other eight have no `links`. A pick on a tilted (3+2) contour is refused too (#1473 item 6).\n\n## Expected\n\n| Kind | Start | Exit | Arm in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Contour5D, MultiAxisContour | a point on the ring | the ring end | 1384, 1950 |\n| Parallel5D, RotaryParallel | the first pass nearest the pick | the last pass | 1395, 1584 |\n| Swarf, AdvancedSwarf | the start of the first swarf pass | the end of the last pass | 1486, 1497 |\n| RotaryContour | an angle on the rotary ring | the exit angle | 1574 |\n| RotaryOffset | a point on the offset ring | the ring end | 1679 |\n| MultiAxisRough | the entry of the first rough level | the last pass | 1777 |\n| Flow5D | the first flow line | the last flow line | 1880 |\n\nThe pick is projected in the tool frame or the rotary frame of the kind (question 1 of #3324).\n\n## Why effort:max\n\nEach kind has its own tilt, shank-avoidance and rotary laws. A user start changes the order and the frame of the path. The first-traverse judge does not read these kinds (`first_traverse.rs:23-27`), so each kind needs its own proof.\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- Shank avoidance and the tilt limit (`max_tilt_deg`) hold at the pick.\n- The rotary clearance holds on the move to the start.\n- The lead room on the ring kinds.\n\n## Done means\n\n- For each kind: a pin test shows the start at the pick, a pin test shows the exit, and a pin test shows an impossible pick refused by name. A kind that cannot take a pick has a row that says so by name.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous path. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped multi-axis golden without a pick is byte-identical.\n- Work it in slices, one kind for each PR. This issue may be split further.\n\nSafety floor: this changes toolpaths, collision results and posted G-code.\n",
